WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.452
Marilla opened the door. She saw the odd girl in the ugly dress, with long red braids and big eyes.

2
00:00:09.453 --> 00:00:14.645
"Matthew Cuthbert, who’s that?" she said. "Where’s the boy?"

3
00:00:14.646 --> 00:00:19.480
"There wasn’t any boy," said Matthew slowly. "There was only her."

4
00:00:19.481 --> 00:00:24.425
He nodded at the child. He realized he didn't even know her name.

5
00:00:24.426 --> 00:00:32.420
"No boy? But there must be a boy!" insisted Marilla. "We asked Mrs. Spencer for a boy."

6
00:00:32.421 --> 00:00:39.563
"Well, I asked the stationmaster, and Mrs. Spencer didn’t bring a boy," said Matthew. "I had to bring the girl home."

7
00:00:39.564 --> 00:00:43.693
"Well, what do we do now?" asked Marilla.

8
00:00:43.694 --> 00:00:47.044
During this conversation the child was silent.

9
00:00:47.045 --> 00:00:49.892
Suddenly she understood what was happening.

10
00:00:49.893 --> 00:00:55.518
"You don’t want me!" she cried. "You don’t want me because I’m not a boy!

11
00:00:55.519 --> 00:01:01.754
I should have known. Nobody ever did want me!" She burst into tears.

12
00:01:01.755 --> 00:01:05.925
Neither Marilla nor Matthew knew what to do.

13
00:01:05.926 --> 00:01:11.574
Finally Marilla said, "Well, well, there’s no need to cry.

14
00:01:11.575 --> 00:01:17.581
You can stay here until we find out what happened. What’s your name?"

15
00:01:17.582 --> 00:01:23.047
The child stopped crying and asked eagerly, "Will you please call me Cordelia?"

16
00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:28.012
"Call you Cordelia? Is that your name?" asked Marilla.

17
00:01:28.013 --> 00:01:35.305
"No, it’s not exactly my name, but I would love to be called Cordelia. It’s a beautiful name."

18
00:01:35.306 --> 00:01:41.440
"I don’t know what you mean. If Cordelia isn’t your name, what is?" Marilla asked.

19
00:01:41.441 --> 00:01:47.923
"Anne Shirley," the girl answered. "But Anne is such an unromantic name."

20
00:01:47.924 --> 00:01:52.483
"Anne is a good, plain, sensible name," said Marilla.

21
00:01:52.484 --> 00:01:55.859
"It’s all right, but I like Cordelia better.

22
00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:01.467
If you must call me Anne, please call me Anne spelled with an ‘e’," Anne said.

23
00:02:01.468 --> 00:02:07.538
"What does it matter how it’s spelled?" asked Marilla, trying to stop a smile.

24
00:02:07.539 --> 00:02:17.667
"Oh, it looks so much nicer. A-n-n looks horrible, but A-n-n-e looks more distinguished."

25
00:02:17.668 --> 00:02:23.820
"Did Mrs. Spencer bring any other orphans besides you?" Marilla inquired.

26
00:02:23.821 --> 00:02:27.740
"She brought Lily Jones for herself," Anne answered.

27
00:02:27.741 --> 00:02:32.291
"Lily is only five years old, and she is very beautiful.

28
00:02:32.292 --> 00:02:39.082
She has nut-brown hair. If I were very beautiful and had nut-brown hair, would you keep me?"

29
00:02:39.083 --> 00:02:43.247
"No. We want a boy to help Matthew on the farm.

30
00:02:43.248 --> 00:02:48.939
A girl is no use. Now take off your hat, and let’s eat dinner."

31
00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:54.026
Anne took off her hat, and they sat down to eat. But Anne could not eat.

32
00:02:54.027 --> 00:02:58.172
She nibbled at the bread and butter, and nibbled at the apple pie.

33
00:02:58.173 --> 00:03:02.244
When dinner was finished, Marilla showed Anne to a spare bedroom.

34
00:03:02.245 --> 00:03:06.377
Anne got into bed and put her head right under the covers.

35
00:03:06.378 --> 00:03:11.078
"Good night," Marilla said a little awkwardly but kindly.

36
00:03:11.079 --> 00:03:20.296
Suddenly Anne’s head reappeared. "How can you say it’s a good night when you know it’s the worst night I’ve ever had?" she cried.

37
00:03:20.297 --> 00:03:23.049
She disappeared under the covers again.

38
00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:26.874
Marilla went into the kitchen and started to wash the dishes.

39
00:03:26.875 --> 00:03:30.106
Matthew sat on a chair, saying nothing.

40
00:03:30.107 --> 00:03:34.770
"One of us will have to take the girl back tomorrow," said Marilla.

41
00:03:34.771 --> 00:03:38.357
"I suppose so," said Matthew reluctantly.

42
00:03:38.358 --> 00:03:43.531
"You suppose so!" Marilla echoed. "Don’t you know so?"

43
00:03:43.532 --> 00:03:46.769
"Well now, she’s a real nice little thing, Marilla.

44
00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:51.987
It’s a pity to send her back. She likes it so much here," said Matthew.

45
00:03:51.988 --> 00:03:58.614
"Matthew Cuthbert! Do you really think we should keep her?" said Marilla, astonished.

46
00:03:58.615 --> 00:04:03.115
"Well, no . . . not exactly," stammered Matthew.

47
00:04:03.116 --> 00:04:06.832
"Of course we cannot keep her," said Marilla.

48
00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:09.206
"What good would she be to us?"

49
00:04:09.207 --> 00:04:13.239
"We might be some good to her," said Matthew unexpectedly.

50
00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:19.613
"Matthew Cuthbert, I can see that you want to keep her. That girl has bewitched you!"

51
00:04:19.614 --> 00:04:23.689
"Well now, she’s a real interesting little thing," said Matthew.

52
00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:26.499
"You should have heard her talk, coming from the station."

53
00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:31.642
"Oh, she can talk all right. I don’t like children that talk so much.

54
00:04:31.643 --> 00:04:36.627
I don’t want an orphan girl, and if I did, it wouldn’t be her."

55
00:04:36.628 --> 00:04:40.049
The next morning Anne awoke and sat up in bed.

56
00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:43.151
For a moment she couldn’t remember where she was.

57
00:04:43.152 --> 00:04:47.650
First she had a delightful thrill, and then a horrible memory.

58
00:04:47.651 --> 00:04:52.997
This was Green Gables, and they didn’t want her because she wasn’t a boy!

59
00:04:52.998 --> 00:04:56.305
She got dressed and went downstairs for breakfast.

60
00:04:56.306 --> 00:04:59.404
"I’m pretty hungry this morning," she announced.

61
00:04:59.405 --> 00:05:04.474
"I’m glad it’s such a sunny morning. But I like rainy mornings as well.

62
00:05:04.475 --> 00:05:07.850
All sorts of mornings are interesting, don’t you think?

63
00:05:07.851 --> 00:05:12.348
You don’t know what’s going to happen throughout the day. Anything could happen!"

64
00:05:12.349 --> 00:05:16.141
"For goodness sake, be quiet!" said Marilla.

65
00:05:16.142 --> 00:05:20.280
Anne obeyed and was so silent that it made Marilla nervous.

66
00:05:20.281 --> 00:05:26.439
Matthew was also quiet, but this was natural, so the meal was a very silent one.

67
00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:32.555
After breakfast Anne washed the dishes, and then Marilla told her to go and play outside.

68
00:05:32.556 --> 00:05:39.496
Anne ran to the door, excited. Then she stopped suddenly, came back, and sat at the table.

69
00:05:39.497 --> 00:05:42.597
"What’s the matter now?" said Marilla.

70
00:05:42.598 --> 00:05:48.425
"I can’t go out," said Anne. "It’s no use loving Green Gables.

71
00:05:48.426 --> 00:05:54.402
If I go out and meet all those trees and flowers, it’ll just be harder to leave."

72
00:05:54.403 --> 00:05:59.875
Marilla thought, "In all my life, I never saw or heard anything like it!

73
00:05:59.876 --> 00:06:03.189
She is kind of interesting, as Matthew says.

74
00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:06.153
I am already wondering what she’ll say next."

75
00:06:06.154 --> 00:06:11.939
But when evening came, Marilla and Anne got in the buggy and left Green Gables.

76
00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:24.986
They were on their way to Mrs. Spencer’s house.

